Yep, that's the behaviour here too. If you set:
OPTIONS=name:player
[i.e as though you wanted a character named 'player']
It will work 'almost-properly':

When you start MacNetHack, and there are no saved games, you'll get 
the "New Player" dialog, with _no_ name supplied.

If there are saved games you'll get the "Quit/New/Load<choices>" 
dialog. And loading will work as you would expect. ['New' works as 
above]

The occasional new game will still give you a character other than 
your choice in the dialog. This is a known bug [Q341-1, listed in 
the QT bugs at www.nethack.org], marked as Fixed (=in some future 
release). 

